    weft_rvv.block_five_bit_qh_source brick, naming the 32-bit qh field bytes -- the
    5th-bit source is operand/source-driven, NOT a descriptor-baked byte offset on
    THIS op), TWO typed SIGNED/SIGNLESS i8 LMUL m1 !weft_rvv.vector PLAIN-int8
    activation operands (the q8 low half paired with the low nibbles, the q8 high
    half with the high nibbles), and the active !weft_rvv.vl token. It carries an
    explicit operation kind and product relation, and produces ONE widened i16 LMUL
    m2 !weft_rvv.vector result holding the sum of the low and high five-bit
    asymmetric widening products.

